WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.300
The point first: five ways a message fails.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:09.560
Fajar sends his manager a careful update: three hundred words, in the order things happened.

3
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:15.250
She reads two lines and replies: so, are we on track?

4
00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:21.850
What she understood is what he communicated.

5
00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:31.120
A message can fail in five ways. Burying the lead. The curse of knowledge. Wrong altitude. Monologue. And stakes freeze: fluent with friends, rigid when it matters.

6
00:00:31.520 --> 00:00:40.875
At work, people want the point first and the journey second. So he rewrites it. The point, the reason, and the decision he needs from her.

7
00:00:41.275 --> 00:00:49.175
You can audit any message with three questions. Does the first sentence carry the point? Could a smart outsider follow it without your context? And did you ask anything that checked what they understood?

8
00:00:49.575 --> 00:00:56.575
What they understood is what you communicated. Put the point first, the journey second.

9
00:00:56.975 --> 00:01:01.375
Now it is your turn. Take the last important message you sent and score it against the five challenges.
